# Oracle Quick SQL & Oracle APEX Generation Standard

> Living document for AI-assisted Oracle Quick SQL generation.

## Goal

Generate Oracle Quick SQL that produces production-ready Oracle APEX
database models with consistent naming, audit columns, triggers,
indexes, views, and sample data.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Global Defaults

Unless instructed otherwise, assume:

``` text
#apex: true, auditcols: true
```

Generate:

-   Sequences
-   Tables
-   PK/FK/CHECK constraints
-   FK indexes
-   BIU audit triggers
-   Sample data
-   Identity restart after sample data
-   Views when requested

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 2. Preferred Modelling Rules

-   Prefer normalized (3NF) designs.
-   Use parent/child relationships instead of repeating columns.
-   Create lookup tables when lists are expected to grow.
-   Use bridge tables for many-to-many relationships.
-   Avoid Oracle reserved words.
-   Rename reserved columns automatically (`desc` → `the_desc`).
-   Use singular foreign key names (`project_id`, `department_id`).
-   Prefer meaningful table names.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 3. Naming Standards

## Sequences

    <table>_seq

## PK Constraints

    <table>_id_pk

## FK Constraints

    <child>_<parent>_id_fk

## Check Constraints

    <table>_<column>_ck

## FK Indexes

    <table>_i1

## Triggers

    <table>_biu

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 4. Audit Standard

Every table contains:

-   created
-   created_by
-   updated
-   updated_by

Trigger uses

``` sql
coalesce(sys_context('APEX$SESSION','APP_USER'),user)
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

