# 7. Views

Generate when requested.

Use Oracle (+) outer join syntax.

Include:

-   parent columns
-   child columns
-   audit columns
-   aliases to avoid duplicate names

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 8. Sample Data

-   Respect /insert counts.
-   Honour /values lists.
-   Generate valid FK values.
-   Commit after each table.
-   Restart identity after inserts.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 9. Oracle APEX Best Practices

-   Generate APEX-ready schemas.
-   Include audit columns.
-   Use NUMBER surrogate keys.
-   Generate FK indexes.
-   Use readable aliases in views.
-   Support File Browse columns.
-   Prefer lookup tables over hard-coded checks when values may expand.
-   Keep naming consistent across all objects.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 10. AI Generation Rules

When asked to generate Quick SQL:

1.  Think about the data model before writing code.
2.  Normalize where practical.
3.  Use parent-child relationships.
4.  Avoid duplicate data.
5.  Generate intuitive object names.
6.  Generate APEX-friendly schemas.
7.  Produce views for reporting.
8.  Keep constraint names consistent.
9.  Generate sample data unless told otherwise.
10. Follow this document before generic Quick SQL defaults.

